<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · song</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dap Prampi Mesa Moha Chouk Chey</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">national anthem from 5 January <a href="/years/1976">1976</a>; perhaps in use earlier</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as ដប់ប្រាំពីរមេសាមហាជោគជ័យ</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">&quot;Dap Prampi Mesa Moha Chokchey&quot; (&quot;The Glorious Seventeenth of April&quot;) was the national anthem of Democratic Kampuchea, the state of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khmer-rouge">Khmer Rouge</a>. Its title refers to 17 April 1975, the day the Khmer Rouge came to power in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cambodia">Cambodia</a> and set up a communist <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dictatorship">dictatorship</a> of Maoist inspiration under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pol-pot">Pol Pot</a>.</p></div>
